'''''Claoxylon''''' is a [[flowering plant]] [[genus]] in the [[Euphorbia|spurge]] [[Family (taxonomy)|family]], [[Euphorbiaceae]], comprising [[dioecious]] [[subshrub]]s to small trees. It was first described as a genus in 1824.<ref>Jussieu, Adrien Henri Laurent de. 1824.  De Euphorbiacearum Generibus Medicisque earumdem viribus tentamen, tabulis aeneis 18 illustratum 43, pl. 14, f. 43</ref> The genus is distributed in [[paleotropical]] areas: [[Madagascar]] through [[South Asia|South]] and [[Southeast Asia]], [[Malesia]] to [[Melanesia]], [[Hawaii|Hawai{{okina}}i]], and [[Australia]]. Half of the species are in [[Malesia]].

